# The build context, kept to what the Dockerfile actually COPYs.
#
# .venv is the reason this file exists. It is a virtualenv built on a laptop —
# tens of megabytes, and currently broken besides: its interpreter symlink
# points at Indic_scholarship/AI/.venv/bin/python3.14, a path that stopped
# existing when the directory was renamed. Shipping it to the Docker daemon
# costs seconds on every build and could only ever confuse the image.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Secrets. The Dockerfile copies neither, but a build context is not a private
# thing — anything in it can be read out of the image's history by whoever can
# pull the image, so the safe place for it is "not in the context at all".
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Run state: seen URLs and proposals from local CLI runs. Nothing the service
# reads — it holds no state — and a stale seen.json baked into an image would
# be actively wrong.
state/

# Tests and the CLI pipeline stay out for the same reason the Dockerfile does
# not COPY them: generate_enums.py reads the backend's migrations, which are not
# in this context, so a file that cannot run is a file somebody will try to run.
test_*.py
pipeline.py
generate_enums.py

.git/
.github/
